Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||01-03-2001||02:44 AM||||I need some help . I'm looking for coil overs for the front of my 86 GT. I have looked at ryanes site , unfortunaltey there full custom front end is out of my price range at the moment. The problem is ... My suspension works great on the track but on the street it bangs on the bump stops. I have konis up front now with carrera springs , the car is set up wth a bit of rake so the front is a bit lower . it handles with the smallest hint of understeer , which I can dial out with the rear suspension (coil overs , koni's ect) in any case I want coil overs up front<P>any suggestions??<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||01-03-2001||09:22 AM||||Get out your welder and go to town.||||reg||1
Z||000002||VISCERAL||01-03-2001||11:07 AM||||Try these guys.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>1987 Fiero GT: silver, 5 spd, centerforce dual friction clutch, Koni's all around, coilovers in the rear, lowered 2" - susp.tech, poly bushings-control arms-sway bars-cradle-motor, rear sway bar, pioneer cd player, 180 stat, 176-166 fan switch, Rodney Dickman's short shifter, bushings, etc..., grand am brakes all around, k&n filter, next year V-8 + lowered spindles + 17x8 and 17x9" Mas Italy wheels +  235/45/17 and 255/40/17's + new paint + Mr. Mikes leather interior + 11.25" brakes w/ parking brake.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Wade87GT||01-05-2001||10:12 AM||||Here's a few words from Shelby Custom's website regarding their dropped lower control arms, "Have you ever ridden in a lowered car that rides like a bull, bottoming out on every little bump in the road. This can happen if you cut down your factory coils or use lowered coils. Believe me, my first Diablo replica was a teeth chipping ride with shortened coils in the front!" Slammed, my car rides exactly like yours and I'm using RCC coilovers all around with a 1" lowering. Superb ride and handling on the highway and smooth roads (I also have the tubular control arms with poly bushings)but it bottoms out going over half inch bumps. I thought I did alot of research on this beforehand, but I didn't find any negative info such as the bottoming out of the suspenion. If I were to do it again, I'd go with either the dropped spindles or the lowered control arms.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||01-05-2001||11:46 AM||||RCC offers a front coil-over kit.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||01-05-2001||04:07 PM||||The bumpstops need to be trimmed or relocated when the car is lowered to prevent them from hitting all the time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||dman||01-05-2001||04:57 PM||||Hello everyone. Rockcrawl gives good advice, to see one way of achieving this check out the following web page:<BR> <A HREF="http://www2.famvid.com/mwons/355SUS.HTM.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www2.famvid.com/mwons/355SUS.HTM.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wade87GT||01-06-2001||06:50 PM||||The RCC kit requires removel of the metal bump stop cones so that the coil-overs can be installed in their place. Thereafter, the shocks and/or the springs are now your "bumpstops".||||reg||1
Z||000008||lowCG||01-08-2001||02:29 AM||||I wouldn't bother with lowered control arms,as the geometry isn't going to change,only the spring location.<BR>Try the search function to locate a procedure that's been documented/tried/tested that'll help you do what you want;a guy with a 355 replica has it in detail on his website after I described it here about a year ago.<BR>What's the advertised rate of your Carrera springs?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wade87GT||01-08-2001||09:08 AM||||I have HAL springs which are rated at 300 and the Carrera shocks are set at the #2 position.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tigger||01-08-2001||10:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wade87GT:<BR><B>If I were to do it again, I'd go with either the dropped spindles or the lowered control arms.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><A HREF="http://www.iserv.net/~strdream/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Street Dreams</A> is making 2" drop spindles for 84-87 Fieros.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||01-08-2001||11:28 AM||||Thanks for all the info , Like I said earlier My car bangs on the front and is terrible for street driving. Get it on a track and it's a pleasure to drive. But I do drive it on the street, and on long trips , 10 hours to fierolisa's house in Ohio was a back wrenching ride (but worth it) I'm always amazed at porsche 911's , ride so smooth , even in race form , a little harsh but nothing in comparison. I still haven't decided between drop spindles and coil overs , which is best for racing useage?? The car sees autocrosses and track events.<P>Thanks <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slammed Fiero||01-08-2001||11:31 AM||||On the carrera front springs , I forget the rate I have it written downb somewhere , If memory serves me It's a little heavier than stock , but not by much (15-20lbs) I have found a fiero (84-87) works best with a relatively soft front end.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
